@@@ problem 36 valid-sudoku
title: Valid Sudoku
difficulty: Medium
topics: Array, Hash Table, Matrix
params: board
time: O(1)
space: O(1)
bench: off

=== description
Decide whether a partially filled `9 x 9` Sudoku board is **valid**. Only the filled cells need to follow the rules:

- each row contains the digits `1-9` at most once;
- each column contains the digits `1-9` at most once;
- each of the nine `3 x 3` sub-boxes contains the digits `1-9` at most once.

A valid board is not necessarily solvable. Empty cells are `'.'`.

=== constraints
- `board.length == 9`, `board[i].length == 9`
- `board[i][j]` is a digit `1-9` or `'.'`

=== hints
- Keep three sets of "seen" flags: one per row, one per column, one per box.
- Box index of cell `(r, c)` is `(r / 3) * 3 + c / 3`.

=== template
class Solution {
public:
    bool isValidSudoku(vector<vector<char>>& board) {

    }
};

=== driver
LC_DRIVER {
    h.solve(&Solution::isValidSudoku);
    h.gen([](lc::Gen &g, int) {
        auto digits = g.perm(9, 1);
        std::vector<std::vector<char>> b(9, std::vector<char>(9, '.'));
        for (int r = 0; r < 9; ++r)
            for (int c = 0; c < 9; ++c)
                if (g.coin(0.45)) b[r][c] = '0' + digits[(r * 3 + r / 3 + c) % 9];
        int breaks = g.coin(0.5) ? g.irange(1, 2) : 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < breaks; ++i) b[g.irange(0, 8)][g.irange(0, 8)] = '0' + g.irange(1, 9);
        return lc::lines(b);
    });
}

=== approach
Scan every filled cell once and record its digit in three bit masks: one for its row, one for its column and one for its 3×3 box (`box = (r/3)*3 + c/3`). If the digit's bit is already set in any of them, the board is invalid.

The board is always 9×9, so this is constant time and space.

=== solution
class Solution {
public:
    bool isValidSudoku(vector<vector<char>>& board) {
        // Bit d of rows[r] is set when digit d already appears in row r, etc.
        int rows[9] = {0}, cols[9] = {0}, boxes[9] = {0};
        for (int r = 0; r < 9; ++r) {
            for (int c = 0; c < 9; ++c) {
                if (board[r][c] == '.') continue;
                int bit = 1 << (board[r][c] - '0');
                int b = (r / 3) * 3 + c / 3;
                if ((rows[r] & bit) || (cols[c] & bit) || (boxes[b] & bit)) return false;
                rows[r] |= bit;
                cols[c] |= bit;
                boxes[b] |= bit;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
};

